{"user": "was there any way white could have stopped the h1 avalanche once i took a1?", "user_ts": "2026-08-15T00:36:41.180275+00:00", "assistant": "Probably **not, unless White could immediately take h1 or force you away from it**.\n\nOnce you took **a1**, the top edge became anchored: discs connected to that corner can\u2019t be flipped from the left side. If Black then had access to **h1**, taking it makes the whole top edge/corner structure permanent.\n\nWhite\u2019s only real ways to stop it would have been:\n- **take h1 first**, if legal;\n- **avoid giving you a legal h1 move** earlier;\n- or create a **pass/mobility sequence** that forces you to play elsewhere.\n\nIn this final board, Black ended **40\u201324**, so that corner/edge swing was decisive.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-15T00:36:41.180275+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-15T00:36:46.180275+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Common Ground Question": 1, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 2}, "confidence": {"Common Ground Question": 0.3333333333333333, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Common Ground Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle", "Neutral Feedback"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle", "Neutral Feedback"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "Local Justification": 3, "Worked Line": 2, "General Principle": 2, "Neutral Feedback": 2}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "Local Justification": 1.0, "Worked Line": 0.6666666666666666, "General Principle": 0.6666666666666666, "Neutral Feedback": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Board Report", "Local J