{"user": "i thought a piece i just placed couldn't be flipped the very next turn. what rule lets that happen?", "user_ts": "2026-08-15T00:36:56.180275+00:00", "assistant": "There\u2019s **no \u201cnew piece is safe for one turn\u201d rule** in Othello.\n\nRule is: after each move, the player flips **any opponent discs trapped in a straight line** between the disc they just placed and another of their discs.\n\nSo your newly placed **b7** was Black on your turn, but on White\u2019s very next turn it became an **opponent disc**, so White could flip it if their move bracketed it.\n\nOnly **corner discs** are truly permanent because they can\u2019t be bracketed from behind. Here the final board is full: **Black wins 40\u201324**.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-15T00:36:56.180275+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-15T00:37:01.180275+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3, "Think Aloud": 2}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0, "Think Aloud": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle", "Negative Feedback"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle", "Negative Feedback"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "Worked Line": 1, "General Principle": 3, "Local Justification": 2, "Negative Feedback": 2}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "Worked Line": 0.3333333333333333, "General Principle": 1.0, "Local Justification": 0.6666666666666666, "Negative Feedback": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Board Report", "Worked Line", "General Principle"], "ll