{"user": "they forced my last move into g2 automatically because only one square was legal. does that ever hurt my final count, or is it always neutral?", "user_ts": "2026-08-15T00:37:11.180275+00:00", "assistant": "Not always neutral \u2014 but if it\u2019s your **only legal move**, you **must** play it. You only pass when you have **zero** legal moves.\n\nFor the **final move specifically**, it usually helps your count immediately: you place 1 Black disc and flip at least 1 White disc, so Black\u2019s count goes up. But earlier in the endgame, a forced move can still be \u201cbad\u201d because it may hand White the next move/corner.\n\nSo: **not neutral in disc count**, but **not optional**. In this finished board, Black wins **40\u201324**.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-15T00:37:11.180275+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-15T00:37:16.180275+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 2, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 0.6666666666666666, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Local Justification": 1}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Local Justification": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "llama": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "sonnet": ["Board Report", "General Principle"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_u